    <fr:title text="Continuation Semantics">Continuation Semantics</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
  Let <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F\colon  \mathcal {C}^\mathsf {op} \to  \mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex> be a self-adjoint on the right functor, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}(A, FB) \cong  \mathcal {C}(B, FA)]]></fr:tex>.
</html:p>
    <html:p>
  This induces the following situation.
  <html:figure><fr:resource hash="3af43953e9d0f393545fa80263b64acd"><fr:resource-content><html:img src="/3af43953e9d0f393545fa80263b64acd.svg" /></fr:resource-content><fr:resource-source type="latex" part="preamble"><![CDATA[
    \RequirePackage{vc-math,cmll}
  \RequirePackage{quiver}
]]></fr:resource-source><fr:resource-source type="latex" part="body"><![CDATA[
      \begin {tikzcd}
	        && {\mathcal {C}^\mathsf {op}} \\
	        &&&& {\mathcal {C}_V} \\
	        \\
	        {\mathcal {C}_N} \\
	        && {\mathcal {C}}
	        \arrow [""{name=0, anchor=center, inner sep=0}, "{F\bo }"{description}, curve={height=-12pt}, from=1-3, to=4-1]
	        \arrow [""{name=1, anchor=center, inner sep=0}, "F"{description}, curve={height=12pt}, from=1-3, to=5-3]
	        \arrow ["{F^\mathsf {op}\ff }"', hook, from=2-5, to=1-3]
	        \arrow [""{name=2, anchor=center, inner sep=0}, "{k_{F^2}}"{description}, curve={height=-12pt}, from=2-5, to=5-3]
	        \arrow [""{name=3, anchor=center, inner sep=0}, "{{(k_{F^2})}^\mathsf {op}}"{description}, curve={height=-12pt}, from=4-1, to=1-3]
	        \arrow ["{F\ff }"', hook, from=4-1, to=5-3]
	        \arrow [""{name=4, anchor=center, inner sep=0}, "{F^\mathsf {op}}"{description}, curve={height=12pt}, from=5-3, to=1-3]
	        \arrow [""{name=5, anchor=center, inner sep=0}, "{F^\mathsf {op}\bo }"{description}, curve={height=-12pt}, from=5-3, to=2-5]
	        \arrow ["\dashv "{anchor=center, rotate=-25}, draw=none, from=3, to=0]
	        \arrow ["\dashv "{anchor=center, rotate=-180}, draw=none, from=4, to=1]
	        \arrow ["\dashv "{anchor=center, rotate=-27}, draw=none, from=5, to=2]
      \end {tikzcd}
    ]]></fr:resource-source></fr:resource></html:figure></html:p>
    <html:p>
      <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}_{N}(A,B) = \mathcal {C}(FA,FB) \cong  \mathcal {C}(B,F^2A)]]></fr:tex>
    </html:p>
    <html:p>
      <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}_{V}(A,B) = \mathcal {C}(FB,FA) \cong  \mathcal {C}(A,F^2B)]]></fr:tex>
    </html:p>
    <html:p>
  This induces <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F^2]]></fr:tex>, a monad on <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex> and a comonad on <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}^\mathsf {op}]]></fr:tex>.
</html:p>
    <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
      <fr:frontmatter>
        <fr:authors>
          <fr:author>
            <fr:link href="/vikraman/" title="Vikraman Choudhury" uri="https://forest.vikraman.org/vikraman/" display-uri="vikraman" type="local">Vikraman Choudhury</fr:link>
          </fr:author>
        </fr:authors>
        <fr:date>
          <fr:year>2025</fr:year>
          <fr:month>7</fr:month>
          <fr:day>11</fr:day>
        </fr:date>
        <fr:taxon>Example</fr:taxon>
      </fr:frontmatter>
      <fr:mainmatter>
        <html:p>
    In any symmetric monoidal category <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(\mathcal {C}, \otimes , I)]]></fr:tex> with an exponentiating object <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R]]></fr:tex>,
    the functor <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[[(-), R]]]></fr:tex> is self-adjoint on the right. This induces a <fr:link href="/0003/" title="Continuation Monad" uri="https://forest.vikraman.org/0003/" display-uri="0003" type="local">continuation monad or
    double dualization monad</fr:link> on <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex>.
  </html:p>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
    <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
      <fr:frontmatter>
        <fr:authors>
          <fr:author>
            <fr:link href="/vikraman/" title="Vikraman Choudhury" uri="https://forest.vikraman.org/vikraman/" display-uri="vikraman" type="local">Vikraman Choudhury</fr:link>
          </fr:author>
        </fr:authors>
        <fr:date>
          <fr:year>2025</fr:year>
          <fr:month>7</fr:month>
          <fr:day>11</fr:day>
        </fr:date>
        <fr:taxon>Example</fr:taxon>
      </fr:frontmatter>
      <fr:mainmatter>
        <html:p>
    In any distributive category <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(\mathcal {C}, 0, 1, \times , +)]]></fr:tex> with an exponentiating object <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R]]></fr:tex>,
    the functor <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[[(-), R]]]></fr:tex> is self-adjoint on the right, and the full-image of each functor is a
    model of call-by-name and call-by-value classical logic, respectively,
    and their posetal truncations are Boolean algebras.
  </html:p>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
    <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
      <fr:frontmatter>
        <fr:authors>
          <fr:author>
            <fr:link href="/vikraman/" title="Vikraman Choudhury" uri="https://forest.vikraman.org/vikraman/" display-uri="vikraman" type="local">Vikraman Choudhury</fr:link>
          </fr:author>
        </fr:authors>
        <fr:date>
          <fr:year>2025</fr:year>
          <fr:month>7</fr:month>
          <fr:day>11</fr:day>
        </fr:date>
        <fr:taxon>Example</fr:taxon>
      </fr:frontmatter>
      <fr:mainmatter>
        <html:p>
      In any (Lafont) model of classical linear logic <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {L}]]></fr:tex>,
      the category of coalgebras <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {L^{!}}]]></fr:tex> is a distributive category,
      with an exponentiating object <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R = !\bot ]]></fr:tex>,
      with exponentials <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R^A = !A^\bot ]]></fr:tex>.
  </html:p>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
  </fr:mainmatter>
