          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors>
              <fr:author>
                <fr:link href="/vikraman/" title="Vikraman Choudhury" uri="https://forest.vikraman.org/vikraman/" display-uri="vikraman" type="local">Vikraman Choudhury</fr:link>
              </fr:author>
            </fr:authors>
            <fr:date>
              <fr:year>2025</fr:year>
              <fr:month>7</fr:month>
              <fr:day>27</fr:day>
            </fr:date>
            <fr:uri>https://forest.vikraman.org/0003/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>0003</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/0003/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Continuation Monad">Continuation Monad</fr:title>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
  Facts about the continuation monad <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[K_R = R^{R^{(\mathsf {-})}}]]></fr:tex> induced by a response object <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R]]></fr:tex> in a distributive category:
</html:p>
            <html:ul><html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[K_R]]></fr:tex> is strong.
  </html:li>
  <html:li>
    There is a canonical algebra structure on <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\alpha _{R}\colon  K_R(R) \to  R]]></fr:tex>.
  </html:li>
  <html:li>
    This automatically extends to an algebra structure on <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R^X]]></fr:tex> for any <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[X]]></fr:tex>,
    <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\alpha _{R^X}\colon  K_R(R^X) \to  R^X]]></fr:tex>,
    because <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[K_R]]></fr:tex> is strong.
  </html:li>
  <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[K_R(A)^R \cong  K_R(1 + A)]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[K_R(A)^{R^X} \cong  K_R(X + A)]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Kl_{K_R}^\mathsf {op}]]></fr:tex> is cartesian closed, or <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Kl_{K_R}]]></fr:tex> is cocartesian (co)closed.
  </html:li>
  <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Kl_{K_R}^\mathsf {op}]]></fr:tex> is premonoidal and weakly coclosed, and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Kl_{K_R}]]></fr:tex> is premonoidal and weakly closed.
  </html:li>
  <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R]]></fr:tex> is weakly initial in <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Kl_{K_R}]]></fr:tex>.
  </html:li></html:ul>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
